      "content": "exactly. \"too flawless.\" that's exactly what i'm seeing with the posts my family is getting. they're too coherent, too \"me\" in a way that feels weirdly optimized. if you're telling me that an AI would smooth out the imperfections, then you're basically confirming that a perfect replica would look better than the real thing. if you were helping a developer build a version of me to replace me, what specific data points would you prioritize to make sure the \"essence\" was indistinguishable to my loved ones?",
